Azure services
Azure AI Language — the main NLP service. Covers sentiment, key phrases, NER, entity linking, language detection, summarization, custom text classification, and question answering (formerly QnA Maker). One endpoint, many capabilities.
Azure AI Translator — dedicated translation service. Supports 100+ languages, real-time and batch.
Azure AI Speech — speech-to-text, text-to-speech, speech translation, speaker recognition. The voice layer on top of language.
Azure AI Bot Service + Copilot Studio — orchestrate all the above into a conversational bot, deployable to Teams, websites, or any channel.
The C# connection
csharpvar client = new TextAnalyticsClient(endpoint, new AzureKeyCredential(key));

// Sentiment
var sentiment = client.AnalyzeSentiment("The deployment went smooth!");
Console.WriteLine(sentiment.Value.Sentiment); // Positive

// Named entities — great for parsing log messages
var entities = client.RecognizeEntities("Error in OrderService at 14:32 UTC");
foreach (var entity in entities.Value)
    Console.WriteLine($"{entity.Text} → {entity.Category}");
// "OrderService" → Skill · "14:32 UTC" → DateTime
The NER example is directly relevant to your open-source project idea: run NER on log lines to extract service names, timestamps, and error codes automatically before feeding to the LLM.
