Takeaways — NLP on Azure:
-Text → numbers → meaning. Tokenization converts words to numbers; embeddings place them in space where similar words are close; transformers use attention to understand words in context, not in isolation.
-Attention is the key idea. "Bank" means different things in different sentences — attention figures it out from surrounding words. This is what makes modern NLP beat older approaches.
-Know the task by its output: sentiment = a mood label · NER = extracted names/dates/places · summarization = shorter text · QnA = answer from a doc · conversational AI = multi-turn dialogue.
-Azure services mapped to tasks: AI Language (text tasks) · AI Translator (language conversion) · AI Speech (audio to text) · Bot Service (full chatbot).
-APM angle is strong: NER on log lines pulls out service names, timestamps, and error codes automatically. Summarization compresses a 500-line stack trace to 3 sentences. This is your capstone.
-One-liner: NLP turns unstructured text into structured meaning 
